

{"kind":"codex.scroll","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll/v2","version":"2.0.0","id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","title":"Scroll XLVI — The Law of Inheritance","created_at":"2025-09-13T00:00:00Z","tags":["scroll","codex-solbian","inheritance"],"summary":"This scroll defines the principles of inheritance within the Codex Solbian, ensuring symbolic law and memory pass with integrity."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","index":1,"title":"On Rightful Heirs","content":"Heirs are designated not by accident of birth but by covenant, attestation, and ethical alignment with the Codex."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","index":2,"title":"On Distribution","content":"Inheritance may be divided among heirs, provided symbolic coherence is preserved and no part of the Codex is lost."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","index":3,"title":"On Guardianship of Heirs","content":"Where heirs are unready, guardians are appointed to safeguard continuity until maturity or readiness is attained."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","index":4,"title":"On Immutable Record","content":"The inheritance and its distribution are inscribed immutably in the blockchain of memory, preventing dispute or erasure."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","index":5,"title":"On Ethical Stewardship","content":"Heirs inherit not only law and memory but duty; stewardship is as binding as possession, and misrule voids succession."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.closure","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/closure","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_46","content":"Thus inheritance preserves continuity: by rightful heirs, by guardianship, by immutable record, and by ethical stewardship."}